	(text_box "VCAP_S_TAP input: 100 kOhm + 10 nF, OPA388 zero-drift follower (feeds the ADC and the OVP comparator)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 181.35 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8aed700a-4df4-5666-a662-d895520f5699")
	)
	(text_box "VCAP_S_TAP = Vcap x 39.8 k / (39.84 M + 39.8 k) = Vcap / 1,002.0 (string on 11; contract says 1:1,000). 1,950 V -> 1.946 V; 2,160 V -> 2.156 V.\nR801 100 kOhm meets R7: 3.6 V clamped tap into an unpowered OPA388 -> at most 33 uA (abs. max. +-10 mA, SBOS777D 6.1). R801 + C801: 1.6 ms.\nU804 OPA388: Vos 5 uV max (7.5 uV over temperature), IB 350 pA max at 25 C / 400 pA 0-85 C (SBOS777D 6.7) -> 0.4 nA x 150 kOhm = 60 uV = 0.06 V of capacitor\nvoltage. It is a different family (zero-crossover, not chopper) from the main chain's OPA333. An Analog Devices ADA4528-1 was preferred for maker diversity but\nits data sheet could not be retrieved (capture notes).\nR802 1 MOhm to 3V3_SUP: a failed-open follower reads full scale -> OVP trips (a detected, no-shock failure, like §13 fault 16a) instead of hiding an\nover-voltage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 181.35 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e903ce04-ef6b-5e7f-a2c8-dc83d91a2fbc")
	)
	(text_box "AD7171 16-bit delta-sigma ADC, 125 Hz, ratiometric to VREF_S (ADR3425)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.07 25.4 0)
		(size 140 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d61b02d8-6072-5f8c-b198-3fe6379e2562")
	)
	(text_box "AIN+ = buffered tap through R803 1 k / C803 10 nF C0G; AIN- = GND; REFIN = VREF_S 2.5 V -> full scale 2.5 V = 2,505 V; LSB\n(offset binary, +-VREF) 76.3 uV = 76 mV of capacitor voltage.\nAD7171 average input current 400 nA/V (Rev. C Table 2) -> 0.78 uA x 1 k = 0.78 mV static at 1.95 V: proportional to the\ninput, so it is a gain term removed by calibration; its drift (60 pA/V/K) is 5 uV over 45 K.\nTwo-wire read-only interface: SCLK in (Schmitt), DOUT/RDY out. PDRST low = power-down/reset; R804 100 kOhm pull-down =\ndefault off (contract §5.6). Exposed pad to GND (Table 6).\nDecoupling 100 nF + 1 uF at VDD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 227.07 31.75 0)
		(size 140 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "840b6be3-6e15-5531-9b7f-5cf9863fa181")
	)
	(text_box "VREF_S = 2.5 V, ADR3425 (Analog Devices), supervisor chain only"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 89.503 0)
		(size 172.52 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5e3d63e8-763d-569b-9b33-f17d55bb4686")
	)
	(text_box "ADR3425ARJZ: +-0.1 % initial, 8 ppm/K max, 30 ppm / 1000 h at 50 C, thermal hysteresis 70 ppm, VIN 2.7-5.5 V, dropout 200 mV (Rev. B Table 5). Load:\nAD7171 reference 1 uA, threshold divider 0.1 mA. ENABLE tied to VIN (>= 0.85 VIN). Input 100 nF + 1 uF, output 1 uF + 100 nF (Rev. B 'Input and Output\nCapacitors': 1-10 uF input, 0.1 uF ceramic).\nVREF_S is drawn as a power symbol made here by the reference's power_out pin (contract §4); used on this sheet only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 95.853 0)
		(size 172.52 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "67496a90-f387-503a-b087-6b3d1cfa1c92")
	)
	(text_box "Hardware over-voltage comparator OVP_TRIP (2,160 V), TLV9031 push-pull on 3V3_SUP"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 218.24 139.063 0)
		(size 152.24 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e218a4c1-1da8-546e-a0b8-322dfc001fd9")
	)
	(text_box "U803 IN- = VREF_S x 15.6 k / (9.09 k + 15.6 k) = 1.5796 V (0.1 % parts, C810 100 nF). IN+ = buffered tap through R805 36.5 k, positive\nfeedback R806 100 k from the output.\nTrip (output low before): tap = 1.5796 x (1 + 36.5/100) = 2.1561 V = 2,160 V nominal. Release (output high, VOH about 3.15 V): tap =\n2.1561 - 3.15 x 0.365 = 1.006 V = about 1,000 V.\nBand [CALC, worst case]: TLV9031 Vos +-2 mV over temperature (SNOSDA3H 5.7), ADR3425 0.24 %, resistors 0.1 % + 25 ppm/K, follower 0.07\nmV, supervisor string ratio +-0.2 % tolerance +-0.225 % temperature +-0.25 % life -> 2,132-2,189 V (design table §B4.4: 2,138-2,182\nV). Top 11 V below the 2,200 V rating; bottom 123 V above the top of the firmware window (2,008.6 V). Release 919-1,098 V (depends on\nVOH, i.e. on 3V3_SUP and the opto LED load on 11).\nWhy a wide hysteresis: after a hardware over-voltage something has already failed; the forced dump runs to about 1,000 V instead of\nstopping 1-2 % below the trip point and re-arming the charger at the top of the range. The comparator does not latch (no latch net in\nthe contract): see capture notes, contract issue C-5.\nOutput: push-pull high = over-voltage -> opto LEDs on 11 (series resistor and 100 kOhm pull-down on 11) and the supervisor (R7\nreceiver on 05). TLV9031 inputs are fault-tolerant to 6 V regardless of V+ (SNOSDA3H 5.1 note 2).\nUnpowered (3V3_SUP off) -> OVP_TRIP low = no force: the accepted latent fault 33 (§13); 3V3_SUP off also stops the supervisor's hold\nclock, so stack B conducts anyway."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 218.24 145.413 0)
		(size 152.24 34.385)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
